From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Subject: [PATCH] CMakeLists.txt: drop UseMultiArch.cmake

OE handles multilib/multiarch its own way; upstream's UseMultiArch.cmake
module is neither needed nor available in this cross-build context.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific cross-build, multilib is
handled by the OE build system itself, not by this in-tree cmake module]
Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 9485ae5..e7d2eb2 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@ foreach(_root ${CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH})
   string(REPLACE "${_root}" "" kodiplatform_TINYXML_LIBRARIES_EXPORT "${kodiplatform_TINYXML_LIBRARIES_EXPORT}")
 endforeach()

-include(UseMultiArch.cmake)
 include(CheckAtomic.cmake)

 set(kodiplatform_NAME kodiplatform)
